course: dictionary
lesson: 12524
title: Designed: planned and made for a purpose
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Designed» is a word about planning. When someone designs something, they plan it and draw it before they make it. «Mia designed a poster for the school fair.» She drew the plan first, then made the poster.
explain: Designed can also mean made for a purpose. «This bike is designed for small children.» Read the words around it: the bike is made to suit small children. Try your meaning in the sentence: «This bike is made for small children» still makes sense.
explain: Designed can also mean planned on purpose. «The game was designed to make us think.» The words designed to tell you why the game exists. Check the clues: designed for, designed to and designed by each tell you something different.
fact: Designed is the past tense and past participle of design: design, designs, designed, designing.
fact: «Designed» means planned and drawn before being made.
fact: «Designed for» or «designed to» means made for a particular purpose or person.
fact: «Well-designed» means planned carefully so it works well; «badly designed» means it does not work well.
fact: In design and technology, pupils design, make, and then test and improve. They draw plans and choose materials first.
exercise: «Mia designed a poster for the school fair.» What does designed mean here? | Thrown away after the fair | Bought from a shop | *Planned and drawn before it was made
exercise: «This bike is designed for small children.» What does designed for mean? | Too fast to ride | *Made for a particular purpose or person | Painted with bright colours
exercise: «The tent was well-designed, so it kept us dry in the storm.» Which word shows the tent was planned carefully? | kept | tent | *well-designed | storm
test: «The game was designed to make us think.» What does designed to mean here? | Finished before we started | Broken by the rain | *Planned on purpose so that it would make us think
test: Ben says designed means the same as made. What is the best reply? | *Not quite: designed means planned and drawn first, before making | Designed means the opposite of made | Yes, designed and made always mean the same
exam: In «The robot was designed by a team of students», what does designed by tell you? | *Who planned and drew the robot before it was made | Who planned and drew the robot | What colour the robot was | Where the robot was sold
